=== Inclusivity normalization for discrete (INT4) subtype ===
# PG canonicalizes INT4 ranges so the upper bound is
# always exclusive: `[1,10]` becomes `[1,11)`, and
# `(1,10)` becomes `[2,10)`.
SELECT '[1,10]'::INT4RANGE AS inc_inc;
ERROR 1064: You have an error in your SQL syntax; check the manual that corresponds to your MySQL server version for the right syntax to use near '::INT4RANGE AS inc_inc' at line 1
SELECT '(1,10)'::INT4RANGE AS exc_exc;
ERROR 1064: You have an error in your SQL syntax; check the manual that corresponds to your MySQL server version for the right syntax to use near '::INT4RANGE AS exc_exc' at line 1
